{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1552727-obtenebration-homebrew-for-vtr-i-am-working-on","id":1552727,"title":"Obtenebration Homebrew for VTR I am working on","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-07-29T13:13:42-07:00","id":1552727,"title":"Obtenebration Homebrew for VTR I am working on","content":"So, I am working on a homebrew for Obtenebration combining a little bit from the Khaibit, but mostly from the VTM Lasombra and looking at offering it as an alternative discipline for Mekhet (would replace Celerity).<br /> <br /> I tried to keep the more powered up nature of Requiem disciplines in mind, but keep the versatility of Obtenebration which I think was its strong suit. The Khaibit focused on it being used for dealing with ephemerals and for assassination.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Obtenebration</b><br /> <br /> <br /> The Beast demands obedience from all including darkness itself. It slips<br /> into the Kindred\u2019s shadow, twisting it first then extending to the shadows of others. It progresses from the simple forming of shadows, to using them to harm, consume, move, or create.<br /> Obtenebration is the trademark Discipline of clan Mekhet which is the unearthly control over shadows, darkness, and the abyss.<br /> <br /> All but the most basic uses of Obtenebration are clearly supernatural and care must be taken when using it in the presence of mortals, who are filled with dread at the mere sight of it.<br /> <br /> The kindred themselves must also be careful for the shadows are volatile, improper use may see the vampire and not their foes as the one consumed by the darkness.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Panoply</b><br /> <br /> The vampire's shadow warps and twists under the might of the beast, it drapes over them shrouding them in shadow for a moment, and when it pulls back it leaves something behind.<br /> With this treasured discipline the vampire is never unarmed or without protection, just as they are never without their shadow.<br /> <br /> Panoply creates a weapon or suit of armor out of living shadow, the creations can only be simple weapons or armor, a bow and a dozen arrows works as does a suit of chainmail but a gun does not.<br /> <br /> Panoply can create a weapon, and the damage is equivalent to your obtenebration dots, for 2 vitae the damage can be boosted by 1. Weapons made by panoply do aggravated damage to ephemeral entities.<br /> <br /> Panoply can create an armor, with a rating up to your obtenebration dots, for 2 vitae the armor rating can be boosted by 1.<br /> <br /> Weapons and armor created by panoply have a somewhat ethereal quality, they are made up of differing shades of shadow from the deep black to gray to dark purple, not quite see through but not solid in appearance either. The vampire using them must take care to either make them appear mundane through obfuscate or use them only in a situation where there will be no survivors or in one where the survivors cannot recall what they saw.<br /> <br /> Cost: 0 Vitae, (2 conditional)<br /> Dice Pool: Resolve + Occult + Obtenebration<br /> Action: Instant<br /> Duration: Scene<br /> Roll Results<br /> <br /> Dramatic Failure: The vampire not only fails to form a solid feature from shadow, but also takes 1 level of bashing damage from the failed attempt and one level of bashing for any 1's rolled.<br /> <br /> Failure: The vampire cannot manifest the shadows.<br /> <br /> Success: The vampire creates what they desire from the shadows.<br /> <br /> Exceptional Success: The weapon or armor is true shadow, it becomes weightless, and does not lower initiative, defense, or speed.\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Shadowplay</b><br /> <br /> At this level the vampire is not limited to their own shadow. The beast flexes and the shadows of another cower before the might of the beast, the victim's shadow rises from beneath them and chokes the owner with hands of inky blackness, squeezing the life from them in a leeching embrace.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, shadows in the ambient area can be called to make the vampire appear unnaturally sinister, their eyes darken their pallid features stand out in stark relief against inky blackness and the room seems to grow smaller in their presence.<br /> <br /> Choke variant<br /> Cost: 1 Vitae<br /> Dice Pool: Strength + Occult + Obtenebration vs. Stamina +<br /> Blood Potency<br /> Action: Instant<br /> Duration: 1 turn, (2 turns on exceptional success)<br /> Roll Results<br /> <br /> Dramatic Failure: The vampire not only fails to command shadow, but the victims shadow cannot be commanded again for the night.<br /> <br /> Failure: The vampire cannot control the shadows.<br /> <br /> Success: The vampire's mastery of shadow is evident for every success achieved a mortal victim or ephemeral takes 1 health level of lethal damage, a vampire or other supernatural suffers bashing damage instead.<br /> <br /> Exceptional Success: The shadow lingers, binding for a time the character gains the stunned tilt.<br /> <br /> Intimidation variant<br /> Cost: None<br /> Dicepool: None<br /> Action: Instant<br /> Duration: Scene<br /> <br /> The vampire adds their obtenebration dice to any roll that makes use of intimidation.\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Shroud</b><br /> <br /> At this level the kindred are not bound to existing shadow. The Beast demands service from all including darkness itself. It slips into the Kindred\u2019s hand or into their mouth wreathing it in viscous smoke, ready to consume everything. The vampire can expel it to create a cloud of inky blackness within 50 meters of their location. The cloud completely obscures light and even sound to some extent. Those who have been trapped within it (and survived) describe the cloud as viscous and unnerving. This physical manifestation lends credence to those Mekhet who claim that their darkness is something other than mere shadow.<br /> <br /> The tarry mass actually extinguishes light sources it engulfs (with the exception of fire), and muffles sounds until they are indistinguishable. Those within the cloud lose all sense of sight and feel as though they\u2019ve been immersed in pitch. Sound also warps and distorts within the cloud, making it nearly impossible to accomplish anything. Additionally, being surrounded by the Shroud is suffocating as the murk smothers and agitates the victims. More than one unfortunate mortal has \u201cdrowned\u201d in darkness.<br /> <br /> Mekhet can see through their own shroud perfectly.<br /> <br /> Cost: 2 Vitae<br /> Dice Pool: Manipulation+ Occult + Obtenebration<br /> Action: Instant<br /> Duration: Scene<br /> Roll Results<br /> <br /> Dramatic Failure: The vampire not only fails to command shadow, but takes 1 lethal damage and a further 1 lethal damage for every 1 rolled.<br /> <br /> Failure: The vampire cannot control the shadows.<br /> <br /> Success: The vampire's mastery of shadow is evident for every success achieved the shadow is 3 meters in diameter. Those within lose 2 points of stamina mortal victims with 2 stamina or less are killed, a vampire suffers this penalty as a temporary loss of 2 health levels. Those within it are given the blinded, and deafened tilts.<br /> <br /> Exceptional Success: The shadow grows darker and seems to still, characters stuck within the murk gain the leg wrack tilt to one leg finding it difficult to move through the tarry cloud and the stamina damage upgrades from 2 to 3 points.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Shadowstep</b><br /> <br /> <br /> At this level the kindred are not bound to the physical plane as strongly as most. The Beast tears through all including darkness itself. The vampire has such fine control over the darkness that he may become it briefly and reform himself from other darkness close by. The vampire may Shadowstep through walls, floors, and even mystical barriers. The Mekhet simply steps \u201cinto\u201d a shadow and re-emerges from another shadow a short distance away (or next to the barrier, if there is no shadow on the other side.<br /> <br /> Cost: 0<br /> Dice Pool: Dexterity+ Occult + Obtenebration<br /> Action: Instant<br /> Duration: turn<br /> Roll Results<br /> <br /> Dramatic Failure: The vampire not only fails to command shadow but becomes temporarily trapped in the abyss. They will linger in this plane for 1 day plus another day for every 1 rolled, and will lose the regular amount of vitae per day as if they rose normally. Additionally when the time is up they will be spat out in a random location 3 miles away plus an additional 3 miles for every 1 they rolled.<br /> <br /> Failure: The vampire cannot control the shadows.<br /> <br /> Success: The vampire's mastery of shadow is evident for every success achieved the vampire may teleport up to 15 meters.<br /> <br /> Exceptional Success: The trip through the shadows was pleasant the beast gains the sated condition.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Nightshades</b><br /> <br /> At this level the kindred are known to the shadows that serve them. The Beast demands service from all including darkness itself and finally something tangible answers. The vampire has gained such power over Obtenebration's dark energies that he may summon creatures made of shadow itself. There is much debate as to the true nature of these night shades. Some claim they are damned souls brought back to the land of the living. Others state they are animated darkness like the Strix. Still others think of them as extensions of the vampire's own black spirit. A few Mekhet have pointed out that these may all be one and the same... The vampire drips the blood into his own shadow, creating a doorway through which the Shade enters this world. The shade can only emerge from the character's own shadow but may move about freely thereafter. Once created, the shade is ready to serve the Mekhet.<br /> <br /> <br /> Cost: 4 Vitae and 1 temporary willpower dot per shade<br /> Dice Pool: Presence + Occult + Obtenebration<br /> Action: Instant<br /> Duration: Nights equal to obten dots, can be prolonged by this value again by giving it 4 vitae<br /> Roll Results<br /> <br /> Dramatic Failure: The shade forms but attacks its master perhaps immediately perhaps days later, storyteller is encouraged to give no clues about the shades state, but the character may attempt to use auspex if they pass a mental roll of storyteller's choice against the shade.<br /> <br /> Failure: The vampire cannot summon the shade.<br /> <br /> Success: The vampire's mastery of shadow is evident the shade enters ready to serve.<br /> <br /> Exceptional Success: The shade gains an additional point to stamina, and strength.\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Shade stats</b><br /> <br /> Size 5<br /> Speed 11<br /> Defense 4<br /> Armor 0-1 (if using panoply)<br /> Imitative 4<br /> Health 9<br /> Willpower: 5<br /> Physical: Strength 3, Dexterity 3, Stamina 4<br /> Social Composure 1, Manipulation 0, Presence 0<br /> Mental Wits 4, Intelligence 2, resolve 4<br /> Skills: Athletics 1, Melee 3, Occult 3, Stealth 5<br /> Disciplines: Obfuscate 1, obten 1, auspex 1.<br /> <br /> Other Information: A Night Shade is not blinded by light (although flame injures it as does any other attack), and it is not affected by illusions or by darkness, natural or unnatural and can use its disciplines at no cost. Shades are destroyed instantly by direct sunlight.<br /> <br /> <br /> So I am looking for feedback on these I personally do not think they are too strong, at least not in comparison to some other discipline abilities, I am a little unsure about Nightshades though, I wanted a power that served a similar niche as ghouling or familiar with a higher cost but more power but I may lower the stats a tad.<br /> <br /> Panoply is more of a thematic power, a way for a mekhet to appear unarmed but if absolutely necessary brandish equipment that would breach the masquerade if not for obfuscate making it possibly ignored. It is based on an old power <b>Aegis of Shadow </b>that let a vampire create an armor that could soak bashing lethal, and aggravated with the exception of fire and sunlight granting 1 point of this armor for each success on a manipulation and occult roll difficulty 7. The aggravated damage reduction, possibility of a ridiculously good roll and casual fear ability is what made this a level 6 power. Without those aspects I think it scales nicely as a level 1 power a vampiric spy would use.<br /> <br /> Shroud is basically unchanged except for the extra successes giving an advantage and applying mechanical tilts instead of the effects it had in masquerade.<br /> <br /> Shadow step has some mechanical rules that actually give getting trapped in the abyss more downsides. And it was an essential power for an infiltrator, fitting right in as a substitute for protean.<br /> <br /> Shadowplay is perhaps the most changed, I stamina was simply far too weak, so I made it deal actual damage but did make it a contested roll and gave it the downside of in the event of failure it could not be attempted again on the same character.<br /> <br /> If you can think of adjustments or even changing the order or attributes used let me know! <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27607-bloodyrelight","name":"BloodyRelight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27607_2.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-29T13:37:59-07:00","id":1552729,"title":"","content":"Panoply alone is, for generic combat purposes if you are willing to throw away any supernatural subtlety and can spare a moment's preparation, nearly equivalent to having both Vigor and Resilience at your Obtenebration dots, with no activation cost, even before factoring in the powers of the other dots. (It has an optional 2 Vitae cost that is an unimportant side show to its main effect.)<br /> <br /> It's not balanced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-29T16:22:17-07:00","id":1552734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1552727-obtenebration-homebrew-for-vtr-i-am-working-on?p=1552729#post1552729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Panoply alone is, for generic combat purposes if you are willing to throw away any supernatural subtlety and can spare a moment's preparation, nearly equivalent to having both Vigor and Resilience at your Obtenebration dots, with no activation cost, even before factoring in the powers of the other dots. (It has an optional 2 Vitae cost that is an unimportant side show to its main effect.)<br /> <br /> It's not balanced.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hmm... I can see where you are coming from.<br /> <br /> I don't think it is equivalent to vigor and resilience though.<br /> <br /> It does not add additional strength to rolls so it is not equivalent to passive vigor. A vigor user with a comparable weapon which there are many can benefit from those added dots to their strength roll, and furthermore with a cost of 1 vitae can add their vigor to the damage itself of any attack they make. <br /> <br /> it does not add health levels so it is not equivalent to resilience's passive effect it is comparable I suppose to it's active effect for armor, but it is still armor, not the mythical durability of say a vampire so even when it blocks damage you still would take 1 bashing damage as per raw whereas with resilience you would ignore it entirely. It also only covers what a similar set of armor would cover.<br /> <br /> I can definitely see removing the added vitae cost for a plus 1 for either but there are armors and weapons in the game line that are competitive with the ones panoply would grant, it does not start to compete with just wearing plate armor and using obfuscate until 4 dots of obten 3 if you use vitae, for weapons it is the same a greatsword from hurt locker is a plus 4 weapon, and it would still have the disadvantages unless you rolled an exceptional success.<br /> <br /> I could have clarified that a bit more. I will do so, it has to be based on a weapon or armor found in game and gets its penalties and the like from that.<br /> <br /> I could see limiting it to say 3-4 dots, and adding a vitae cost... I think I had my editions mixed up I thought full plate was 6 must have gotten that from masquerade.I will make some edits as that is unbalanced.<br /> <br /> <br /> Let's see...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The vampire's shadow warps and twists under the might of the beast, it drapes over them shrouding them in shadow for a moment, and when it pulls back it leaves something behind.<br /> With this treasured discipline the vampire is never unarmed or without protection, just as they are never without their shadow.<br /> <br /> Panoply creates a weapon or suit of armor out of still shadow, the creations can only be simple weapons or armor, a bow and a dozen arrows works as does a suit of chainmail but a gun does not.<br /> <br /> Panoply can create a piece of equipment up to your obtenebration dots, in general armor or damage, to a maximum of 4 dots.<br /> <br /> The weapon created can match any of mortal make but is limited by the form it takes, a knife would still do the damage of a typical knife 0L. All disadvantages from said weapon apply. Weapons made by panoply do lethal damage to ephemeral entities.<br /> <br /> The armor created can match any mortal make but is limited by the form it takes, chainmail would thus be limited to 3 general and will only cover the areas covered by a set of said armor, all disadvantages from said armor also apply such as still taking 1 point of bashing damage even if the hit is completely absorbed by general armor.<br /> <br /> Weapons and armor created by panoply have a somewhat ethereal quality, they are made up of differing shades of shadow from the deep black to gray to dark purple, not quite see through but not solid in appearance either. The vampire using them must take care to either make them appear mundane through obfuscate or use them only in a situation where there will be no survivors or in one where the survivors cannot recall what they saw.<br /> <br /> Weapons and armor created by panoply must exist in this world and have the penalties of the weapon or armor they are based on. when removed or disarmed (in the case of weapons) the weapon and/or armor vanish.<br /> <br /> Cost: 1 Vitae per weapon or armor created.<br /> Dice Pool: Resolve + Occult + Obtenebration<br /> Action: Instant<br /> Duration: Scene<br /> Roll Results<br /> <br /> Dramatic Failure: The vampire not only fails to form a solid feature from shadow but also takes 1 level of bashing damage from the failed attempt and one level of bashing for any 1's rolled.<br /> <br /> Failure: The vampire cannot manifest the shadows.<br /> <br /> Success: The vampire creates what they desire from the shadows.<br /> <br /> Exceptional Success: Same as above.<br /> <br /> With this at 1 dot the vampire is limited to a 1 lethal or below weapon, and a 1 general armor, armor so heavy hides or linen/padded armor from Dark eras.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27607-bloodyrelight","name":"BloodyRelight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27607_2.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-29T18:02:12-07:00","id":1552739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BloodyRelight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1552727-obtenebration-homebrew-for-vtr-i-am-working-on#post1552727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(would replace Celerity).</div> </div> </div> </div>That would give the Mekhet two exclusive Disciplines, which is potentially powerful. Depending on how much the ST makes it hard to get a teacher on those Disciplines, the difference is even bigger.<br /> <br /> If you do give them <b>Obtenebration</b>, replace <b>Auspex</b>. You can later find a way to reintroduce <b>Auspex</b> into your game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1552727-obtenebration-homebrew-for-vtr-i-am-working-on?p=1552729#post1552729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Panoply alone is, for generic combat purposes if you are willing to throw away any supernatural subtlety and can spare a moment's preparation, nearly equivalent to having both Vigor and Resilience at your Obtenebration dots, with no activation cost, even before factoring in the powers of the other dots. (It has an optional 2 Vitae cost that is an unimportant side show to its main effect.)<br /> <br /> It's not balanced.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27607-bloodyrelight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27607_2.webp');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27607\" data-vbnamecard=\"27607\">BloodyRelight</a> reasoning. <i>Panoply</i> doesn't stack with an actual weapon or armor, nor has passive effects, so I don't think it's particularly powerful. It's actually weak if it can't do better than actually buying equipment with Resources.\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BloodyRelight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1552727-obtenebration-homebrew-for-vtr-i-am-working-on?p=1552734#post1552734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could see limiting it to say 3-4 dots, and adding a vitae cost... I think I had my editions mixed up I thought full plate was 6 must have gotten that from masquerade.I will make some edits as that is unbalanced.</div> </div> </div> </div>The power must be better than simply buying equipment.<br /> <br /> Give it a Vitae cost, that makes a lot of sense, but you not only shouldn't give it a limit, but should also remove or reduce normal penalties. Especially since it can be disarmed without any problem, and if that happens it disappears, demanding paying again and spending a new action.<br /> <br /> Also, remove the roll. Why's there a roll? For some powers, a roll is just added complexity for no payoff, and that's pretty much the case. You pay the cost, you get the shadow equipment.\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BloodyRelight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1552727-obtenebration-homebrew-for-vtr-i-am-working-on#post1552727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Shade stats</b><br /> <br /> Size 5<br /> Speed 11<br /> Defense 4<br /> Armor 0-1 (if using panoply)<br /> Imitative 4<br /> Health 9<br /> Willpower: 5<br /> Physical: Strength 3, Dexterity 3, Stamina 4<br /> Social Composure 1, Manipulation 0, Presence 0<br /> Mental Wits 4, Intelligence 2, resolve 4<br /> Skills: Athletics 1, Melee 3, Occult 3, Stealth 5<br /> Disciplines: Obfuscate 1, obten 1, auspex 1.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the last dot of the Discipline, they're quite weak. Actually scratch that, they're just quite weak.<br /> <br /> Don't give them Discipline dots, though. Give them the direct benefits if you want, but do not name as Disciplines.<br /> <br /> Instead, a better arrangement is for the character to be able to affect them with their own powers, specially from the same Discipline.<br /> <br /> At most I would reduce their Mental Attributes, all of them.<br /> <br /> <br /> On the other powers I have no opinion yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-30T15:14:50-07:00","id":1552753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1552727-obtenebration-homebrew-for-vtr-i-am-working-on?p=1552739#post1552739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That would give the Mekhet two exclusive Disciplines, which is potentially powerful. Depending on how much the ST makes it hard to get a teacher on those Disciplines, the difference is even bigger.<br /> <br /> If you do give them <b>Obtenebration</b>, replace <b>Auspex</b>. You can later find a way to reintroduce <b>Auspex</b> into your game.<br /> <br /> <br /> I actually agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27607-bloodyrelight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27607_2.webp');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27607\" data-vbnamecard=\"27607\">BloodyRelight</a> reasoning. <i>Panoply</i> doesn't stack with an actual weapon or armor, nor has passive effects, so I don't think it's particularly powerful. It's actually weak if it can't do better than actually buying equipment with Resources.<br /> <br /> <br /> The power must be better than simply buying equipment.<br /> <br /> Give it a Vitae cost, that makes a lot of sense, but you not only shouldn't give it a limit, but should also remove or reduce normal penalties. Especially since it can be disarmed without any problem, and if that happens it disappears, demanding paying again and spending a new action.<br /> <br /> Also, remove the roll. Why's there a roll? For some powers, a roll is just added complexity for no payoff, and that's pretty much the case. You pay the cost, you get the shadow equipment.\u200b<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Good to see you are still active monteparnas! Thank you for your feedback, I will try to make some edits as you suggested, the point about the roll is I think a good one looking through the core book many of the powers that require blood do not require one, and it does cost an action.<br /> <br /> On the two signatures that is a good point, maybe I could instead use it as a bloodline with an added bane maybe just port this version of Obtenebration to the Khaibit? That could be an easy fix since they already have the thematic weakness to the light.<br /> <br /> I am in agreement that if that fails it could be given as an alternative option to auspex.<br /> <br /> -----------------------------------<br /> <br /> Panoply<br /> <br /> The vampire's shadow warps and twists under the might of the beast, it drapes over them shrouding them in shadow for a moment, and when it pulls back it leaves something behind.<br /> With this treasured discipline the vampire is never unarmed or without protection, just as they are never without their shadow.<br /> <br /> Panoply creates a weapon or suit of armor out of living shadow, the creations can only be simple weapons or armor, a bow and a dozen arrows works as does a suit of chainmail but a gun does not.<br /> <br /> Panoply can create a piece of equipment up to your Obtenebration dots in general armor or damage.<br /> <br /> The weapon created can match any of mortal make but is limited in some way by the form it takes, a knife would still do the damage of a panoply blade but all disadvantages from said weapon apply. Weapons made by panoply do lethal damage to ephemeral entities.<br /> <br /> The armor created can match any mortal make but is limited by the form it takes, chainmail would still give obtenebration dots in rating to general armor but will only cover the areas covered by a set of said armor, all disadvantages from said armor also apply such as still taking 1 point of bashing damage even if the hit is completely absorbed by general armor.<br /> <br /> Weapons and armor created by panoply must exist in this world and have the penalties of the weapon or armor they are based on. when removed or disarmed (in the case of weapons) the weapon and/or armor vanish. If a weapon made by panoply had a sheathe it can be safely stored on the vampire's person to free the hand.<br /> \u200b<br /> Weapons and armor created by panoply have a somewhat ethereal quality, they are made up of differing shades of shadow from deep black to gray and even dark purple, thy are not quite see through but not solid in appearance either. The vampire using them must take care to either make them appear mundane through obfuscate or use them only in a situation where there will be no survivors or in one where the survivors cannot recall what they saw.<br /> <br /> Cost: 1 Vitae, or (2 Vitae conditional)<br /> Action: Instant<br /> Duration: Scene<br /> <br /> Conditional: The creation is true shadow, it becomes weightless, and does not lower initiative, defense, or speed.\u200b<br /> <br /> -----------------------<br /> <br /> Do you think this is a good compromise or does 2 vitae sound too steep?<br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> ---------------------<br /> <br /> On shades, I originally basically copied the entry from one of my vtm books changing attributes where appropriate, they primarily are used for spying thus their high stealth. I will have to look into revising them to make them worthy of being a fifth dot power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27607-bloodyrelight","name":"BloodyRelight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27607_2.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-30T22:54:00-07:00","id":1552761,"title":"","content":"I personally think 2 Vitae seems too steep, I would keep it at 1 and have all the benefits. It's still a supernatural power, with a cost, and one that won't stack with true equipment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-31T10:11:55-07:00","id":1552775,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">Greeting, as a fellow VTR fan, I\u2019m glad to see some new home brew, keep it alive(or undead)! Here are some of my thoughts.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Panoply : </b>With the new version you posted it thinks it\u2019s fairly balanced, maybe a bit weak. Obfuscate 1 can allow a character to walk around with full military gear with no real risk of getting caught and it grants them the benefit of anonymity as well. Panoply works in reverse; it grants weapons to those who don\u2019t have them but they risk masquerade breach. Additionally, the damage being capped by Obtenebration dots means it requires heavy investment into the discipline to have tangible results. The real advantage I can think of is that it allows Vigour users to go ham on boosting damage without fear of breaking their weapon. Here\u2019s what I wound change :</span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">I would remove the vitae cost entirely. </span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">Remove the need for a dice pool to keep it in line with similar personal buff power. (Protean for instance works like this.)</span></li> </ul><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Shadowplay :</b> Balanced, but imo, kinda boring. Shadowplay should allow an obtenebration user to manipulate shadows and solidify them to some extent. Personally, I would go something like this :</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Shadowplay</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">At this level the vampire is not limited to their own shadow, they can manipulate or grasp things with their shadows. (Feel free to add any more evocative lore text i'm pretty bad at this)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Cost:</b> 2 Vitae (or more, see text)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Dice Pool:</b> None (See text)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Action:</b> Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Duration:</b> One scene</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">When activating shadowplay a vampire can manipulate any surrounding shadows within Obtenebration dots + Blood potency meters for a scene. They can manipulate how shadows manifest themselves, and use them to grasp things as if they were using their own hands. This allows them to manipulate objects, grapple victims, or even manipulate shadows to make themselves more threatening.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">Any active use of Shadowplay takes an instant action and requires instant actions for subsequent turns to keep the effect. The obtenebration user can spend a point of willpower to make one of their manipulation more persistent. </span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Grappling : </b>The vampire can grapple with any character within reach that is in contact with any shadow. The obtenebration users use Strength + Occult + Obtenebration as a dice pool. Vigour does not add to the user's strength pool as usual. (Alternatively you can use strength + occult + vigor dots.) If the vampire uses a point of willpower to keep the effect active the shadow will keep repeating the same grappling action each turn. Finally, when taking the damage move in a grapple against an ephemeral being it deals lethal damage instead of bashing.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Intimidation : </b>If the vampire can add their obtenebration dots to intimidation. If they are wearing panoply armour, they do not need to keep concentrating on their manipulation to keep the intimidation bonus. </span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Shroud : </b>The power is fine, but I don\u2019t get the stamina reduction, maybe lethal or superficial damage would be more appropriate if it\u2019s a life-sucking cloud? It could deal damage whenever a victim starts its turn inside.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Shadow steps : </b>This is fine for a fourth level power, but cost 0 means it can be spammed indefinitely, is this intentional? If the idea is that they can use that power frequently, I would make the vitae cost 1 for a whole scene, this would allow a vampire to teleport frequently but not without cost. I would still have each jump require a roll to activate.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Nightshades :</b> I\u2019m on the fence with this one. The shades are both powerful and kind of weak to me and i have a hard time evaluating it. </span><ul><li>Any \u2018\u2019summons\u2019\u2019 with static stats is going to scale poorly, but they are also in line with animalism.</li> <li>They are good at stealth, kinda meh in a battle and can\u2019t interact socially.</li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">Four Vitae + 1 will is too much. I\u2019d probably go 1 or 2 vitae and 1 will per shades. </span></li> </ul><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">I personally don\u2019t know if I would make summons the \u2018\u2019end game\u2019\u2019 of obtenebration. Maybe I\u2019d buff other disicplines in interesting way, or open a new way to use the discipline, maybe it could allow the user to make shadow tangibles using the user's stamina or resolve dot as hardness for objects, etc. Nightshades could be a good Animalism \u2022</span><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">\u2022</span> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">and Obtenebration \u2022</span>\u200b<span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">\u2022</span>\u200b<span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">\u2022</span>\u200b<span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">\u2022</span>\u200b<span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"> devotion however.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>The Sixth Discipline.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">I agree with @<b><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\">monteparnas</a></b>, giving them obtenebration and auspex would make them for a very powerful clan lorewise, having two unique disciplines would be powerful. However, if there\u2019s one clan that could pull it off narratively is clan Mekhet, as they are considered the weirder clan.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">Here are some of my suggestions :</span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">Make them a bloodline with Auspex, Celerity, Obfuscate, Obtenebration. </span></li> </ul><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">Make them into a Mekhet or Ventrue Bloodline that gains Obtenebration. I can totally see the Ventrue \u2018\u2019Lord of shadow\u2019\u2019 aspect to it, and it makes them closer to actual Lasombra ; Callous with their touchstone, dominate as a discipline, animalism to push others to their worst self, etc. </span></li> </ul><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">Give them Celerity, Obtenebration, Obfuscate and make Auspex a non-clan-specific discipline, granting every clan access to it as an off-clan discipline without needing mekhet blood specifically. This buffs everyone and doesn't remove the discipline. Auspex is often a discipline i find myself wanting with all my characters right there with obfuscate so it makes the choice easier.</span></li> </ul><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">Create a six clan completely that use Auspex. You could take the Jiang Shi (VTR P.255) and replace Obfuscate with Auspex to give them an interesting dynamic as \u2018\u2019seers\u2019\u2019 of death. Or you could give the Jiang Shi obtenebration instead of obfuscate since they are presented as the clan of death. (They seem to have a bit of a clan Giovanni vibe without straight necromancy). </span></li> </ul><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">Rework obtenebration as devotions that only mekhet can feasibly obtain (requiring the most work). Here are some suggestions.</span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Panoply :</b> Auspex \u2022, Obfuscate \u2022 resilience \u2022 </span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Shadowplay :</b> Auspex \u2022, Obfuscate \u2022\u2022, Vigor \u2022</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Shroud : </b>Auspex \u2022\u2022, Obfuscate \u2022\u2022\u2022, Vigor \u2022</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Shadow step : </b>Auspex \u2022, Celerity \u2022 Obfuscate \u2022\u2022\u2022</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Nightshade : </b>Auspex \u2022, Animalism \u2022\u2022, Obfuscate \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</span></li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">Hope this helps! Feel free to use any or nothing at all, those are only my observations and opinions.</span><br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26771-algarik","name":"Algarik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26771_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-31T10:25:22-07:00","id":1552776,"title":"","content":"<b>(My previous post is unnaproved state, please feel free to delete it, i think its because of how i copy pasted another's user's name as a link it flagged it as an exterior link). </b><br /> <br /> <br /> Greeting, as a fellow VTR fan, I\u2019m glad to see some new home brew, keep it alive(or undead)! Here are some of my thoughts.<br /> <br /> <b>Panoply : </b>With the new version you posted it thinks it\u2019s fairly balanced, maybe a bit weak. Obfuscate 1 can allow a character to walk around with full military gear with no real risk of getting caught and it grants them the benefit of anonymity as well. Panoply works in reverse; it grants weapons to those who don\u2019t have them but they risk masquerade breach. Additionally, the damage being capped by Obtenebration dots means it requires heavy investment into the discipline to have tangible results. The real advantage I can think of is that it allows Vigour users to go ham on boosting damage without fear of breaking their weapon. Here\u2019s what I wound change :<ul><li>I would remove the vitae cost entirely.</li> <li>Remove the need for a dice pool to keep it in line with similar personal buff power. (Protean for instance works like this.)</li> </ul><b>Shadowplay :</b> Balanced, but imo, kinda boring. Shadowplay should allow an obtenebration user to manipulate shadows and solidify them to some extent. Personally, I would go something like this :<br /> <br /> <b>Shadowplay</b><br /> At this level the vampire is not limited to their own shadow, they can manipulate or grasp things with their shadows. (Feel free to add any more evocative lore text i'm pretty bad at this)<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 2 Vitae (or more, see text)<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> None (See text)<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Duration:</b> One scene<br /> When activating shadowplay a vampire can manipulate any surrounding shadows within Obtenebration dots + Blood potency meters for a scene. They can manipulate how shadows manifest themselves, and use them to grasp things as if they were using their own hands. This allows them to manipulate objects, grapple victims, or even manipulate shadows to make themselves more threatening.<br /> Any active use of Shadowplay takes an instant action and requires instant actions for subsequent turns to keep the effect. The obtenebration user can spend a point of willpower to make one of their manipulation more persistent.<ul><li><b>Grappling : </b>The vampire can grapple with any character within reach that is in contact with any shadow. The obtenebration users use Strength + Occult + Obtenebration as a dice pool. Vigour does not add to the user's strength pool as usual. (Alternatively you can use strength + occult + vigor dots.) If the vampire uses a point of willpower to keep the effect active the shadow will keep repeating the same grappling action each turn. Finally, when taking the damage move in a grapple against an ephemeral being it deals lethal damage instead of bashing.</li> <li><b>Intimidation : </b>If the vampire can add their obtenebration dots to intimidation. If they are wearing panoply armour, they do not need to keep concentrating on their manipulation to keep the intimidation bonus.</li> </ul><br /> <b>Shroud : </b>The power is fine, but I don\u2019t get the stamina reduction, maybe lethal or superficial damage would be more appropriate if it\u2019s a life-sucking cloud? It could deal damage whenever a victim starts its turn inside.<br /> <br /> <b>Shadow steps : </b>This is fine for a fourth level power, but cost 0 means it can be spammed indefinitely, is this intentional? If the idea is that they can use that power frequently, I would make the vitae cost 1 for a whole scene, this would allow a vampire to teleport frequently but not without cost. I would still have each jump require a roll to activate.<br /> <br /> <b>Nightshades :</b> I\u2019m on the fence with this one. The shades are both powerful and kind of weak to me and i have a hard time evaluating it.<ul><li>Any \u2018\u2019summons\u2019\u2019 with static stats is going to scale poorly, but they are also in line with animalism.</li> <li>They are good at stealth, kinda meh in a battle and can\u2019t interact socially.</li> <li>Four Vitae + 1 will is too much. I\u2019d probably go 1 or 2 vitae and 1 will per shades.</li> </ul>I personally don\u2019t know if I would make summons the \u2018\u2019end game\u2019\u2019 of obtenebration. Maybe I\u2019d buff other disicplines in interesting way, or open a new way to use the discipline, maybe it could allow the user to make shadow tangibles using the user's stamina or resolve dot as hardness for objects, etc. Nightshades could be a good Animalism \u2022\u2022 and Obtenebration \u2022\u2022\u2022\u200b\u2022\u200b devotion however.<br /> <br /> <b>The Sixth Discipline.</b><br /> I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a>, giving them obtenebration and auspex would make them for a very powerful clan lorewise, having two unique disciplines would be powerful. However, if there\u2019s one clan that could pull it off narratively is clan Mekhet, as they are considered the weirder clan.<br /> Here are some of my suggestions :<ul><li>Make them a bloodline with Auspex, Celerity, Obfuscate, Obtenebration.</li> </ul><ul><li>Make them into a Mekhet or Ventrue Bloodline that gains Obtenebration. I can totally see the Ventrue \u2018\u2019Lord of shadow\u2019\u2019 aspect to it, and it makes them closer to actual Lasombra ; Callous with their touchstone, dominate as a discipline, animalism to push others to their worst self, etc.</li> </ul><ul><li>Give them Celerity, Obtenebration, Obfuscate and make Auspex a non-clan-specific discipline, granting every clan access to it as an off-clan discipline without needing mekhet blood specifically. This buffs everyone and doesn't remove the discipline. Auspex is often a discipline i find myself wanting with all my characters right there with obfuscate so it makes the choice easier.</li> </ul><ul><li>Create a six clan completely that use Auspex. You could take the Jiang Shi (VTR P.255) and replace Obfuscate with Auspex to give them an interesting dynamic as \u2018\u2019seers\u2019\u2019 of death. Or you could give the Jiang Shi obtenebration instead of obfuscate since they are presented as the clan of death. (They seem to have a bit of a clan Giovanni vibe without straight necromancy).</li> </ul><ul><li>Rework obtenebration as devotions that only mekhet can feasibly obtain (requiring the most work). Here are some suggestions.<ul><li><b>Panoply :</b> Auspex \u2022, Obfuscate \u2022 resilience \u2022</li> <li><b>Shadowplay :</b> Auspex \u2022, Obfuscate \u2022\u2022, Vigor \u2022</li> <li><b>Shroud : </b>Auspex \u2022\u2022, Obfuscate \u2022\u2022\u2022, Vigor \u2022</li> <li><b>Shadow step : </b>Auspex \u2022, Celerity \u2022 Obfuscate \u2022\u2022\u2022</li> <li><b>Nightshade : </b>Auspex \u2022, Animalism \u2022\u2022, Obfuscate \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> Hope this helps! Feel free to use any or nothing at all, those are only my observations and opinions.<br /> \u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26771-algarik","name":"Algarik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26771_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-31T18:55:33-07:00","id":1552789,"title":"","content":"My initial thought was to make <b>Auspex</b> into a non-specific discipline open for everyone (I'm also prone to always buying it regardless), but I think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26771-algarik\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26771_1.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26771\" data-vbnamecard=\"26771\">Algarik</a>'s idea of making them into <i>Devotions</i>is a really good one.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't even make them exclusive to the Mekhet, although I would probably make them a secret of some specific group. Only they can teach Obtenebration Devotions, and they hunt tirelessly anyone who stoles their secrets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-01T07:04:50-07:00","id":1552802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1552727-obtenebration-homebrew-for-vtr-i-am-working-on?p=1552789#post1552789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't even make them exclusive to the Mekhet, although I would probably make them a secret of some specific group. Only they can teach Obtenebration Devotions, and they hunt tirelessly anyone who stoles their secrets.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yes, a small and secretive covenant with obtenebration devotions could be pretty cool. They could focus on hunting strixes, hence their very secretive nature, they do not want to be infiltrated by them which could spell their doom. Bonus point if their leader is actually a strix using kindred to dispatch rivals, or just enjoy the fun of spreading chaos like strixes tends to do. It does make obtenebration a bit harder to obtain or justify for some character, which might or might not be the goal here.<br /> <br /> I think the strong point for making obtenebration a collection of secretive devotions is that while all powers are shadow themes, they remain somewhat disconnected. Sure they all involve shadows, but there's little connection to each other like some discipline like Auspex, Dominate, Majesty, or Obfuscate have.<br /> <br /> Although, there's a point to be made that not all discipline dots build on their previous foundation, animalism probably being the worst offender by having their dots fourth and fifth dot going in a completely different direction than previous dots.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\">As a fun thought exercise, this is how I would rework auspex as a general discipline with the base clans.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Daeva :</b> Auspex, Celerity, Majesty </span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Reasoning :</b> Auspex really fits Daeva becoming obessive with their target, and makes them scarier. They know your vulnerability and know how to use it. It let them celerity instead of Vigor because I can\u2019t think of any clan, outside of mekhet, that really fits the celerity vibe and I already changed them quite a bite bellow. Besides, it makes daevas into Anne Rice vampires, so why not.</span></span></li> </ul><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Gangrel :</b> Auspex, Animalism, Protean</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Reasoning : </b>Gangrel is my least favourite clan, not because they aren\u2019t cool, but because I always feel like they can\u2019t really get out of the solo-survivor vibe and contribute to a political game. They are supposed to be the clan that adapt to anything but can't meaningfully do so in one of the main game pillars. Protean is already a pretty much a physical discipline so why not give them sharp hunter senses that they can use to adapt to social settings. It just makes sense to me. </span></span></li> </ul><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Mekhet :</b> Obtenebration, Obfuscate, Resilience (or vigor)</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Reasoning : </b>This change clan mekhet quite a bit, but it gives them the creeping shadow vibe you just can\u2019t get rid of. Vigor could make sense if using the vigor variant of shadowplay I posted earlier. It might make them a bit too nosferatu-like, however. Finally, I removed auspex as I thought it made more sense for Gangrel and Daeva to have with this rework. </span></span></li> </ul><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Nosferatu :</b> Nightmare, Vigor, Obfuscate</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Reasoning :</b> Clan Nosferatu is perfect, fight me.</span></span></li> </ul><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Ventrue :</b> Animalism, Dominate, Vigor (or resilience)</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos\"><b>Reasoning :</b> I get that the Lords are really based on their VTM predecessor, so resilience was expected, but I never quite fully bought into the \u2018\u2019control of self\u2019\u2019 aspect to explain Resilience. It's fine, i don't hate it, but Ventrue have very oppressive power by nature and vigor quite fit that aspect and it makes them cooler. It also ties them to Julii who had Dominate, Resilience and vigor. We could thematically explain the shift to animalism by explaining that they had to adapt to the strixes hunt by learning to control beasts to defend themselves and their territories. If mekhets gain vigor instead, ventrues can keep resilience.</span></span></li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26771-algarik","name":"Algarik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26771_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}